      ],
      "depiction": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/docs/cat-harness/assets/img/workflows/methodology-from-source.svg",
      "description": "Adopt the method of a shared paper, book or standard: origin and licence, ingestion, what is adopted and refused, placement by ownership, integration by calling existing processes, and the owner's review. The general process an agent follows when someone shares a paper, book or standard and asks for its method to be used: establish origin and licence, ingest it, render what the method says with what is adopted and refused, place it by ownership, integrate it into the processes that already exist by calling them rather than copying them, make every skill and tool it uses a declared Tool, relate it to existing beans and issues, and put the adoption to the owner. Written 2026-09-23 while adopting WireGen (arXiv:2312.07755) as the worked case. Operating skill: adopt-methodology-from-source; the adoption rules themselves are folio-assistant's methodology-adoption.",
      "enforcement": "strict",
      "flowCount": 12,
      "inSubgraph": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness.jsonld#directory/processes",
      "name": "Adopt a methodology from a source document",
      "nodeCount": 12,
