      ],
      "depiction": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/docs/cat-harness/assets/img/workflows/translation-workflow.svg",
      "description": "The machine half of translation, end to end: extract the translatable strings, inject a catalogue back, check the result by back-translating it, and track whether the source has moved since.\n\nYou are in this process whenever translation happens without a person having to be present. Two of its steps are the exception and are drawn in their own lane: a flagged passage is ADJUDICATED by a human, and a translation becomes official only when a human signs it off. `human-translation-workflow` is what happens when a person is doing the translating rather than checking it.\n\nStaleness is an END state that re-enters at the beginning, not a failure. A source change does not invalidate a translation's accuracy; it invalidates its currency, which is a different fact and is why it is recorded rather than thrown away.",
      "enforcement": "strict",
      "flowCount": 18,
      "inSubgraph": "https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/cat-harness.jsonld#directory/processes",
      "name": "Translation Workflow",
